<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">combat</ansi>

Combat in DOGMud features a tactical, skill-based system with layered defenses, special
moves, and resource management. Understanding these mechanics is key to survival.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Starting Combat ━━━</ansi>

Use <ansi fg="command">attack <target></ansi> to engage in combat. Once started, combat continues each
round until someone flees or dies. See <ansi fg="command">help attack</ansi> for details.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Attack Mechanics ━━━</ansi>

Your attack success is based on:
  - <ansi fg="stat">Combat Skill:</ansi> Weapon Combat (armed) or Unarmed Combat
  - <ansi fg="stat">Dexterity:</ansi> Affects accuracy
  - <ansi fg="stat">Stamina:</ansi> Low stamina (<50%) reduces hit chance and damage

<ansi fg="red">Critical Hits:</ansi> Skill advantage increases crit chance
<ansi fg="red">Fumbles:</ansi> Always ~2.5% chance to completely miss

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Layered Defense System ━━━</ansi>

When attacked, you get multiple chances to avoid damage (in order):

  1. <ansi fg="stat">Dodge:</ansi> Unarmed Combat + Dexterity
     - Available to everyone, costs 2 stamina
     - Reduced by heavy armor and encumbrance

  2. <ansi fg="stat">Parry:</ansi> Weapon Combat + weapon parry rating
     - Only with a weapon equipped, costs 4 stamina
     - Two-handed weapons get bonus

  3. <ansi fg="stat">Block:</ansi> Weapon Combat + shield block rating
     - Only with a shield equipped, costs 5 stamina
     - Most stamina-intensive but effective

First successful defense avoids the attack. Each defense costs stamina, so long fights
become wars of attrition. Run out of stamina and your defenses collapse!

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Dual Wielding ━━━</ansi>

Wield two weapons for extra attacks, but with tradeoffs:
  - <ansi fg="stat">Extra Attacks:</ansi> Offhand weapon gets reduced attacks (×0.5 base)
  - <ansi fg="stat">Accuracy Penalty:</ansi> -10 to hit with offhand attacks
  - <ansi fg="stat">Skill Progression:</ansi> Both weapons train your combat skill
  - <ansi fg="stat">Defense:</ansi> Can parry with either weapon

Use <ansi fg="command">dual-wield</ansi> to toggle dual wielding mode.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Unarmed Combat ━━━</ansi>

Fighting without weapons scales with skill:
  - <ansi fg="stat">Base Damage:</ansi> Low early, scales with Unarmed Combat skill
  - <ansi fg="stat">Attacks:</ansi> 1 attack base, up to 4 attacks at high skill
  - <ansi fg="stat">Special Moves:</ansi> Trip and kick use Unarmed Combat
  - <ansi fg="stat">Defense:</ansi> Can only dodge (no parry/block)

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Special Combat Moves ━━━</ansi>

Tactical moves with cooldowns that can turn the tide of battle:

  <ansi fg="command">bash</ansi>   - Shield bash (50% damage, 40% knockdown, requires shield)
  <ansi fg="command">trip</ansi>   - Leg sweep (25% damage, 60% knockdown, tactical)
  <ansi fg="command">kick</ansi>   - Power kick (40% damage, 35% knockdown, balanced)

All three share a <ansi fg="red">5-round cooldown</ansi>. Choose wisely! Successful knockdowns
apply the <ansi fg="red">prone</ansi> condition. See <ansi fg="command">help prone</ansi> for details.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Target Switching ━━━</ansi>

In combat with multiple enemies, you can switch targets:
  - Use <ansi fg="command">attack <new-target></ansi> to retarget mid-combat
  - Automatic targeting when your current target dies
  - Party members can coordinate on the same target

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Resource Management ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="stat">Stamina:</ansi>
    - Used for: Defenses, special moves, standing up
    - Regenerates slowly during combat
    - Low stamina (<50%) imposes severe penalties
    - Manage carefully in long fights!

  <ansi fg="stat">Health:</ansi>
    - Reach 0 health and you're downed (unconscious)
    - Recover slowly or use healing items/spells
    - Death possible if downed too long

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Ending Combat ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">flee</ansi>      - Attempt to escape (costs stamina, may fail)
  Victory       - Kill or down all opponents
  Defeat        - Reach 0 health (downed state)

